  "foaf:name": "Mapping ecological substrates in the global ocean",
  "sdo:name": "Mapping ecological substrates in the global ocean",
  "sdo:description": "Despite decades of marine surveys and research, systemic understanding of seafloor habitats remains limited. Lack of a unified ecological substrate map hinders exploration of seafloor processes. The Mapping Ecological Substrates in the Global Ocean (MAPS-GO) project aims, through international collaboration, to create a digital global ocean ecological substrate map and database by 2030 that will illustrate distribution patterns, evolutionary trends of the seafloor material and its ecological impacts. MAPS-GO will establish a universal classification of ecological substrates and data standards, integrating public and unlocked legacy data. MAPS-GO will also analyze archived samples and participate in ongoing marine bottom investigations, boost mapping efficiency using advanced technologies including machine learning, intelligent inversion and modeling. This initiative empowers resource development, ecosystem protection, and governance, directly advancing the UN Ocean Decade vision.",
